<title>FINLAND: Stockmann says '96 department store sales up 9 pct.</title>
<headline>Stockmann says '96 department store sales up 9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish retailing group Oy Stockmann Ab said on Friday its full-year 1996 domestic department store sales grew nine percent to 2.5 billion markka.</p>
<p>&quot;Last year, domestic department store sales grew nine percent to 2.5 billion markka,&quot; Hannu Penttila, director of Stockmann's department store division, told Reuters by telephone.  </p>
<p>Department store sales made up 42.6 percent of Stockmann's 6.2 billion markka 1995 group sales.</p>
<p>--Veera Heinonen, Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 240</p>
